From 5a14aee43cae93eaa8371fd9fb58e6de5925b1d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:03:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 135/137] video: the host chooses its video players' hwdec and
 interop

Every video player (a video texture, a video wallpaper) asked libmpv for `hwdec=auto` and left `gpu-hwdec-interop` at
its default, which for the render API means trying every interop libmpv has when the player's render context is made:
on an NVIDIA machine with libcuda reachable that loads the CUDA interop (a CUDA context) and the drmprime one, and
tries VAAPI, Vulkan and drmprime-overlay, which fail without their display or renderer. A host that already decides
how its own players decode had no way to make the core's players follow it, nor to keep them to copy modes.

wp_context_set_video_hwdec (context, hwdec, interop) stores libmpv's `hwdec` and `gpu-hwdec-interop` values on the
context; GLPlayer sets both as options before mpv_initialize, so the render context loads only that interop (`no`:
none). NULL leaves a value at libmpv's default, so a host that never calls it sees no change.

Measured with liascape's scene worker (two 1080p video textures, NVIDIA, `cuda` with `nvdec,nvdec-copy,vaapi-copy,
auto-copy`): each player loads only the CUDA interop and decodes with nvdec, as before; the worker's VRAM stays 906
MiB, since the interops it no longer tries held no device memory. What a video costs is its CUDA context (mpv's CUDA
interop creates one in every render context, 160 MiB here) plus its decoder's surfaces and textures.

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/TODO.md #104 (scene video texture VRAM)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
